Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:28:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] ALFA cards v4: calibration on the v2 ARC reconstruction
 (T15/T17)

The full-sim reconstruction placed the pixel centre on the mid-plane of the 2 mm SiPM, 1 mm behind the face where the
photons are detected; v2 uses the face. Same cell-averaged samples (T06b Xe 2 bar, T06c C4F10), same fit procedure.
GasSigmaSingle 3.005 -> 1.837 mrad (Xe 2 bar), 3.056 -> 1.892 mrad (C4F10); the correlated term roughly halves;
N_sat 10.43 -> 10.33 and 10.24 -> 10.16; yield, efficiency and BendingCoefficient (0.155 / 0.147) essentially unchanged.
make_cards.py reads campaign_v2/calib/{Xe2bar,C4F10}/calib_t06b.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KP5vqAGH2XiGXWtPhaonke
